  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p><strong>Mirror Lake</strong> is a 4,100-foot destination in California. The Mirror Lake Loop covers 5.0 miles (loop) with about 100 feet of elevation gain \u2014 a gradual walk with modest climbing.</p>\n  <h3>The Route</h3><p>Along the way the route passes a spring (Iron Spring) near mile 0.45, a cave (Indian Cave) near mile 0.65 \u2014 useful checkpoints for judging your pace.</p>\n  <h3>Getting There</h3><p>The trailhead is at <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=37.73978,-119.55985\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">37.73978, -119.55985</a> (tap for driving directions). It's roughly 125 miles south of Reno, Nevada. Parking: Mirror Lake parking or shuttle stop. Fee: $35 park entrance.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>Late May through October is the main season. Snow and ice linger into spring and return early in fall at this latitude and elevation; in winter this becomes a different, more serious undertaking requiring traction devices and warm layers.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>The Easy rating comes from the National Park Service difficulty formula, which weighs total distance against elevation gain. Most hikers should budget about 2.5 hours of moving time; add margin for breaks, photos and the descent. Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from National Park Service - Yosemite.</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Half Dome, Vernal Fall and Nevada Fall \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
